Memory search covers people/, projects/, companies/, history/ (every brief ever run), and last_brief.md. Use it first — it's fast and may answer the question without any live queries. Then layer in live Slack/Granola only if more recency is needed.

**"What did I promise X?"** → memory search first (`"X commitment"`), then Granola for recent meetings with X, then Slack `from:me to:X`

**"What does X owe me?"** → memory search for X (`open commitments` surface automatically), then Granola if needed

**"What's the status of Y?"** → memory search for Y first, then Slack + Granola for live signal

**"Who should I talk to about Z?"** → memory search for Z (surfaces people + projects that mention it), cross-reference stakeholders.md

**"What's on my calendar today/this week?"** → `{{CALENDAR_PREFIX}}list_events`

**"What fires are there right now?"** → read last_brief.md fires + search Slack for recent messages from key stakeholders in your tier 1 list

